# Coverage for the code that decides whether a merge may happen. Line coverage,
# matching lemonfiber's 100%-on-applicable-code standard (Q-R61). The __main__
# guards only run when a script is executed rather than imported for test, so
# they are excluded.
#
# `source` rather than `include`, which is the difference between measuring a
# directory and measuring whatever happened to be imported. Under `include`, a
# file nothing imported is absent from the report entirely — so `what_is_blocking.py`
# sat in that list with a suite of eighty-three tests that no workflow ran, and
# the gate reported 100% and meant it, about the other files. Under `source` an
# unimported file is reported at 0% and fails, which is the answer that was wanted.
#
# What `omit` holds is therefore the declared exceptions and nothing else: the
# suites themselves, and the scripts `test_coverage_reads_every_script.py`
# declares unmeasured with a reason. That file compares the two, so a name can be
# dropped from neither quietly.
[run]
source =
    scripts
    shared/gates
omit =
    scripts/test_*.py
    scripts/gen_board.py
    scripts/gen_codeowners.py
    scripts/gen_roadmap_table.py
    scripts/rfc_scaffold.py

[report]
exclude_also =
    if __name__ == .__main__.:
